{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Choosing Destinations","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"text":" is a plain sink: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:)"},{"text":" hands it each batch of records. Traffluent ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"few, each in a module of its own, so an app links only the ones it uses.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Logs-and-traces","text":"Logs and traces","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To see events beside your logs or traces, deliver to ","type":"text"},{"code":"LoggerDestination(logger:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations"},{"text":") or ","type":"text"},{"code":"SpanEventDestination(tracer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Only apps that use swift-log or swift-distributed-tracing this way link them. A span event joins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the span that was active when the event was tracked, even if delivery runs later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-server","text":"A server","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send batches to a server, deliver to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination(endpoint:headerFields:encoder:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":"). It posts each batch as one request whose body is what your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes for it, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is yours. A failed send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is logged and dropped, without holding up the other destinations. It sends with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, or through any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport:"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The bootstrapped tracing instrument, or the one you pass as ","type":"text"},{"code":"instrument:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", injects the trace","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context of the batch’s first record into the request’s header fields, so a server that extracts it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"joins the request to the app’s trace. The encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" always wins, and with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instrument bootstrapped no header is added. Only the first record’s context travels in the header","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields; write each record’s context into the body if the server needs it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to a self-hosted TraffluentCollector, give "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder(plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":") as its encoder, and the collector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API key as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization: Bearer"},{"type":"text","text":" header field. It writes the collector’s ingest format: each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s identifier (which a redelivered record keeps), its name, timestamp and redelivery marker,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its properties read through the event’s schema in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":", and its standard context and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trace context. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is sent only while the record reveals it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Memory","text":"Memory","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To read what was tracked inside the app, deliver to an ","type":"text"},{"code":"InMemoryDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as well (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"): for an event inspector in a debug build, a recent-activity view, a SwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preview, or a test of what your code tracks. It keeps the newest 1,000 records, or as many as you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass as ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", dropping the oldest across batches; ","type":"text"},{"code":"InMemoryDestination.unbounded()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every one. Read it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"events(of: SignedUp.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"records","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"batches","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or wait on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"deliveries","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which announces each batch to one reader.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Sensitive-values-and-call-sites","text":"Sensitive values and call sites","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A property that destinations shouldn’t see unless they must is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. A destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads it only through the record, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"reveal(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and printing or mirroring it shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"<redacted>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes a destination’s records reveal nothing, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"droppingCallSite()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes their call sites. Every other destination receives both:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct SignedIn: Event {","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}","","let backend = InMemoryDestination()","let vendor = InMemoryDestination()","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","    to: backend,","    vendor.redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite()",")","tracker.track(SignedIn(email: Sensitive(\"ada@example.com\")))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let event = backend.events(of: SignedIn.self)[0]","let email = backend.records[0].reveal(event.email)    \/\/ \"ada@example.com\"","let redacted = vendor.records[0].reveal(event.email)  \/\/ nil","let callSite = vendor.records[0].sourceLocation       \/\/ nil"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" narrows a destination to the consent categories it serves (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","abstract":[],"title":"CollectorEncoding","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do."}],"title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","abstract":[{"text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"title":"Tracking Events","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","abstract":[],"title":"TracingDestinations","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","url":"\/documentation\/destinations","abstract":[],"title":"Destinations","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","abstract":[{"text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked.","type":"text"}],"title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","title":"LoggingDestinations","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","title":"Consent Gating","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"}}}